course: dictionary
lesson: 16141
title: Widespread: found in many places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how far something reaches, and widespread is one of them. Wide means large across an area, and spread means something has moved out to cover a space. Together they mean found in many places or among many people. «There was widespread flooding after the storm.» The flooding was not in one street. It covered a big area, so widespread means spread over a large area.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «A widespread belief» tells you that many people believe the same thing. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. "A belief that many people hold" still makes sense, so you have got it right.
explain: Widespread is not always good or bad. «The team had widespread support» means many people backed them. «Widespread damage» means harm in lots of places. The feeling of good or bad comes from the other words in the sentence, not from widespread itself.
fact: Widespread means found in many places or among many people.
fact: «Widespread flooding» means flooding over a large area.
fact: «A widespread myth» is a belief that many people wrongly think is true.
fact: In science, a widespread species is one that lives in many countries.
fact: Widespread can describe good things too, such as «widespread support».
exercise: «There was widespread flooding after the storm.» What does widespread mean here? | Very quiet and calm | Tiny and hidden in one small room | Only in one street | *Found in many places, covering a large area
exercise: Which word could replace widespread in «a widespread illness»? | sleepy | hidden | tiny | *common among many people
exercise: «The team had widespread support from fans across the country.» Does widespread mean the support came from many people? | No, it came from only one person | *Yes, it came from many people | It means the team lost | It means the fans were asleep
test: Which word means found in many places? | cosy | sleepy | tiny | *widespread
test: A widespread myth is | a kind of weather | a very long word | a fact that only one scientist knows | *a belief that many people wrongly think is true
exam: «Widespread support» means | no support at all | support that is hidden away | support from only one person | *support from many people
